 "notes": "Libretto by Emanuel Schikaneder (1791). Words as printed in the Edition Peters vocal score, which the app follows where it differs from the libretto: the old spellings \"Muth\", \"Wuth\", \"Füsse\", \"grösser\", \"hieher\", \"lass\", \"dass\" and \"Sclaven\", \"Flötenton\" in one word (the libretto has \"der Flöte Ton\"), Monostatos's \"Wart', ich will euch Mores weisen\" (the libretto has \"wart', man wird euch Mores weisen\") and \"gehört, noch geseh'n\" (the libretto has \"gehört und gesehn\"), the \"la la ra\" syllables as the print has them, and the repeats of the music (\"sonst erwischen\", \"nur geschwinde\", \"Stille\", \"wer viel wagt\", \"Mores weisen\", \"He! ihr Sclaven, kommt herbei!\", Pamina's \"besten, besten\"), sung as the print has them. In bar 34 the print gives Pamina's syllable as \"gè-\" (with a grave accent; Papageno's is \"ge-\"); it is kept as printed and sung as \"geschwinde\". The slaves' chorus (tenors and basses), who sing \"Das klinget so herrlich\" with Monostatos, is heard with the piano and has no phrases here. IPA follows sung German stage diction: final -er, -ern as [ɐ]; the prefixes er-, ver-, zer- with [ɛr]; r elsewhere rolled or flipped; ch as [ç] after front vowels and [x] after back vowels; glottal stops [ʔ] before initial vowels; final b d g devoiced.",
